 36S  c  1970Gr02: E=28.9 MeV deuteron beam was provided from the University of 
 36S 2c  Michigan 83-inch cyclotron. Targets were 90-|mg/cm{+2} NaCl enriched to
 36S 3c  99.3% in {+37}Cl, vacuum-evaporated onto thin carbon backings.         
 36S 4c  Recoiling {+3}He ions were detected using a 100-|mm |DE and 500-|mm E  
 36S 5c  surface-barrier detector telescope consisting with FWHM=110 keV). For  
 36S 6c  {+3}He ions reaction angles |q>12|', they were detected by Ilford K0   
 36S 7c  nuclear emulsion plates at the image surface of a three-stage magnetic 
 36S 8c  spectrograph with FWHM=25 keV). At at extreme forward angles |q>2.5|', 
 36S 9c  {+3}He ions were detected using a 14|*50 mmposition-sensitive detector.
 36S Ac  Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, |p, and     
