 36S Cc  1968Gr04, a short letter by the same group.                            
 36S  c  1969Pu03: E=23.35 MeV deuteron beam was provided from the Argonne      
 36S 2c  cyclotron. The target was enriched {+35}Cl lead chloride on thin C     
 36S 3c  backing. Reaction products were detected using a |DE-E counter covering
 36S 4c  the angular domain from 12|' to 30|'. Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q).       
 36S 5c  Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, |p, and C{+2}S from the zero-range     
 36S 6c  JULIE-DWBA analysis of the angular distributions.                      
 36S  c  1962Cu07: E=15 MeV deuteron beam was provided from the University of   
 36S 2c  Pittsburgh cyclotron. The target was 2.71-|mg/cm{+2} C{-2}H{-4}Cl{-2}  
 36S 3c  (dichloroethane) with evaporated Au. Recoiling {+3}He ions were        
 36S 4c  analyzed by a magnetic spectrometer and detected using a CsI           
 36S 5c  scintillation crystal at the focal plane. Measured Q value and         
 36S 6c  |s(E({+3}He),|q) of the 36S g.s.                                       
